+# Production hardening baseline
+
+This repository keeps the thesis primitive unchanged: one AES-GCM-SIV message over the
+Zstandard-compressed byte stream, with RFC 8452 POLYVAL semantics. Production hardening must not
+silently turn Zstd frame boundaries or POLYVAL execution segments into independent AEAD messages.
+
+## Security invariants
+
+- Configuration loading is fail-closed. Invalid config/secret permissions abort startup.
+- Direct REST CPU/storage routes require the configured bearer token; only health and crypto-mode
+  discovery are public. The web console requires a valid session for non-discovery API work.
+- Accepted connection tasks are bounded and request headers/buffered JSON bodies have deadlines.
+- CPU-heavy research endpoints use a global non-blocking admission gate before Rayon/spawn_blocking.
+- Duplicate `Content-Length`, unsupported `Transfer-Encoding`, oversized headers and malformed
+  sealed-stream integer fields fail before expensive work.
+- Object plaintext is released only after AES-GCM-SIV authentication succeeds.
+- IPFS blocks are verified by CID before use. Repair writes only bytes that hash to the canonical
+  CID, so physical replica repair does not create a new logical object/root.
+- A catalog write failure is reconciled before IPFS compensation. Ambiguous state keeps the pin;
+  a confirmed absent metadata row is rolled back by unpinning the newly published object.
+- Live secrets must not be tracked by Git; `scripts/check_workspace.sh` enforces this when run in a
+  Git worktree.
+
+## POLYVAL execution
+
+The production/thesis path uses a fused ordered divide-and-conquer reducer. It hashes small runs of
+adjacent segments at tree leaves and combines `left.combine(right)` in stream order. This preserves
+RFC 8452 output while avoiding the primary path's previous `Vec<PolyvalPart>` allocation proportional
+to segment count. The old parallel-local + linear reducer remains as a benchmark baseline.
+
+## Release gate
+
+Use the pinned `rust-toolchain.toml` and committed `Cargo.lock`:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/check_workspace.sh --root . --mode release
+cargo audit
+```
+
+A production release must also exercise live Kubo/database integration in the deployment environment,
+including interrupted upload, backend outage, catalog failure/reconciliation, corrupted block/tag,
+large-object limits, and concurrent-client saturation.
